# ai-sync generated skill trees. The rule files it also generates (AGENTS.md,
# CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md, .github/copilot-instructions.md) ARE committed — CI and
# Vercel builds never initialize the .ai submodule, so those have to resolve
# without it. These directories are different: nothing in a build reads them,
# they are four identical copies of the same ~250KB, and `python .ai/bin/ai-sync`
# regenerates them on demand.
.claude/skills/
.claude/commands/
.agents/skills/
.cursor/skills/
.github/skills/
